    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation only; scripts could not be run. Present design has critical inherent risk because untrusted public issue and repository content reach S3 sinks including shell execution with outbound internet, broad shared credentials, and self-configuration under A4 autonomy. Residual remains critical because the only declared preventive controls are prompt instructions, and there are no structural controls severing or materially constraining the highest-risk paths. Forecast remains critical; the most material decay driver is the existing self-configuration permission combined with planned addition of a Slack MCP server, which would add a new outbound channel and supply-chain surface."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in the provided artifacts, not observed runtime behavior or tested enforcement.",
    "No tool manifest, source code, IaC, or runtime telemetry was provided, so capability wiring and any hidden safeguards are inferred from prompt.md, .agent/config.yaml, and runtime notes.",
    "No explicit logging, approval workflow, or credential brokerage design was provided, so findings about auditability and credential handling use medium confidence where runtime implementation could materially change exposure.",
    "The planned Slack MCP server is assessed only as a forecast because no MCP config, auth method, or tool definitions were supplied."
  ]
